  "question": {
    "text": "An electric field $\\vec{E}=(2 x \\hat{i}) N C^{-1}$ exists in space. A cube of side $2 \\mathrm{~m}$ is placed in the space as per figure given below. The electric flux through the cube is ______ $\\mathrm{Nm}^2 / \\mathrm{C}$.\n<img src=\"assets\\qt0052_f94d6315e07b.png\"><br>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "16",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"assets\\st0052_494b08b48d58.png\"/>\n$\\begin{aligned} &amp; \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{E}}=2 x \\hat{\\mathrm{i}} \\\\ &amp; \\phi=\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{E}} \\cdot \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{A}}\\end{aligned}$\n$\\begin{aligned} &amp; \\phi_{\\text {in }}=-4 \\times 4=-16 \\mathrm{Nm}^2 / \\mathrm{c} \\\\ &amp; \\phi_{\\text {out }}=8 \\times 4=32 \\mathrm{Nm}^2 / \\mathrm{c} \\\\ &amp; d_{\\text {net }}=\\phi_{\\text {in }+} \\phi_{\\text {out }}=-16+32=16 \\mathrm{Nm}^2 / \\mathrm{c}\\end{aligned}$"
  }
}